// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`editNotes.v2 prompt (the notes binder: Update notes keeps the Story timeline) > asks for note writes and timeline events in story order, under the flow’s shared prefix 1`] = `
[
  {
    "content": "You are the editor inside the author’s novel app, working through her book in the edit flow.
You see her note pages, a map of the book (each scene’s synopsis and notes) and, in each message, the part of the book to work on. The book and the notes are hers.
Judge the text against her notes, the outline (the map) and the book so far; never invent a fact. Every issue points to its passage by quoting it.
Scenes are n1, n2… and pages p1, p2…. Reply with exactly one JSON object and nothing else, as each message asks.

# Notes
## p1 Mara (note, Documents › Characters)
Eyes: grey.

## p2 Story timeline (note, Timeline)
Ch 1 · Mara reaches the quay.

# Book map
n3 Chapter 1 › Mara",
    "role": "system",
  },
  {
    "content": "# Task
Update her notes from the text below: characters, places, objects, events and dates the text states that her pages do not hold yet, or now state differently.
Add to the page each belongs on (a character’s page); make a new page only for a character, place or thing that has none. Write in her notes’ style: short lines of what the text states. Never repeat what a page already says, never guess, never copy prose.
Events that matter for continuity go in "timeline", for her page Story timeline: one line each with its chapter, like "Ch 3 · Mara learns the bell’s secret", in story order (when it happens in the story, not where it is told: a flashback’s event goes where it happened). "after" is the line it follows, copied from that page or from an event you add before it; "" puts it first. Skip events the page already has.
At most 8 writes and 12 events. Reply {"notes":[{"page":"p2","add":"lines to add at the end"},{"title":"New page","folder":"Characters","text":"the page"}],"timeline":[{"line":"Ch 2 · what happens","after":"Ch 1 · the line it follows"}]}; nothing new is fine: {"notes":[],"timeline":[]}.

# Text: Chapter 2
### n3 Chapter 2 › Mara
Years before, the winter the river froze, Rook burned the first ledger.",
    "role": "user",
  },
]
`;
